# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Firebase (Auth + Firestore)
#
# MEROS uses Firebase Authentication for Google sign-in and Cloud
# Firestore to store user progress, comments, and the leaderboard.
#
# If these vars are left blank, the app still works as a local-only
# (guest) experience — the login page hides the Google button with a
# friendly notice, and all data stays in browser localStorage.
#
# ── Setup (~5 min, free tier) ──
#   1.   → create project
#   2. Build → Authentication → Sign-in method → enable Google
#   3. Build → Firestore Database → create (production mode, region
#      europe-west* for Uzbekistan latency)
#   4. Paste these Firestore Rules (Rules tab → Edit rules):
#
#        rules_version = '2';
#        service cloud.firestore {
#          match /databases/{database}/documents {
#            match /users/{uid} {
#              allow read: if true;
#              allow write: if request.auth.uid == uid;
#            }
#          }
#        }
#
#   5. Project Settings → General → "Your apps" → Web → register app
#      → copy the config object values into the vars below.
#   6. Authentication → Settings → Authorized domains → add your
#      production domain (e.g. education-project-theta.vercel.app)
#   7. Rename this file to `.env`, restart `npm run dev`.
#   8. For production: add the same vars in Vercel (Project → Settings
#      → Environment Variables) then redeploy.
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=
VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=
